00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.550 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  did you know that there are two pirates  of the caribbean scripts currently in  development so could jack sparrow fans  see johnny depp reprise his iconic role  now that his defamation trial against  ex-wife amber heard is over the answer  may surprise you  finally after more than a month of  deliberation the jury hearing johnny  depp and amber heard's competing  defamation lawsuits has reached a  verdict to briefly recap heard and depp  were married from 2015 to 2017 and heard  alleges that depp was abusive to her  during this time in 2018 heard  identified herself as a public figure  representing domestic abuse in an essay  for the washington post  depp characterized allegations as a hoax  and claims that heard of being the one  abusing him  i can't say that i'm embarrassed because  i know that i'm doing the right thing  depp then claims that the allegation  caused him to lose out on lucrative  acting roles in late 2018 depp sued  heard in virginia for defamation seeking  50 million dollars in damages  the impact on deb's career is central to  his lawsuit under questioning from his  own lawyer depp claims that disney  dropped him from the pirates of the  caribbean franchise after heard's essay  was published heard responded with a  counter suit over depp's hoax  allegations claiming that depp  orchestrated a campaign to get her fired  from aquaman and from her job as a  l'oreal spokesperson depp already lost a  similar defamation lawsuit in the united  kingdom in november 2020 and an appeal  over that decision the following march  however on june 1st 2022 the american  jury sided with depp on all three counts  of defamation  awarding him 15 million dollars in  compensatory and punitive damages the  jury also upheld one of herd's claims of  defamation awarding her 2 million  dollars in compensatory damages now that  the verdict is in here's how it could  affect dep's role in the pirates of the  caribbean franchise going forward  currently there are two pirates of the  caribbean scripts in development which  would make the sixth and seventh  installments in the franchise producer  jerry bruckheimer spoke about johnny  depp's future as jack sparrow weeks  before the verdict was reached  when asked if disney was planning to  cast depp in the sixth film brackheimer  responded not at this point  as it turns out though there might not  be a need for depp embarrassed to the  caribbean six anyway bruckheimer also  revealed that the script is centered on  a female lead with margot robbie in mind  that would seem to eliminate the need  for jack sparrow to factor into the  story on the other hand the seventh film  isn't centered around robbie's possible  character which could leave room for  jack sparrow to return in some capacity  bruckheimer added that the future is yet  to be decided so bruckheimer was already  leaving the door open for a possible  depth return before the verdict was  reached script specifics aside the  biggest question is whether disney wants  to work with depp again or not the  travel has undoubtedly tarnished depp's  reputation still bruckheimer's comments  don't explicitly rule out dep's  potential return therefore there's no  guarantee depp will ever play jack  sparrow again  but it sounds like it hasn't been ruled  out at the same time it's important to  consider that disney is only half of the  equation johnny depp may not even want  to come back as jack sparrow after all  he's gone through and how his  relationship with the walt disney  company has shifted in recent years in  fact during the trial depp confirmed  previous testimony that his connection  with the company has changed so  drastically that he wouldn't return to  the role no matter how much disney  offered  nothing on this earth would get you to  go back and work with disney on a  pirates of the caribbean film that is  true mr rottenborn the actor explained  during his trial testimony there was a  deep and distinct sense of feeling  betrayed by the people that i've worked  hard for people that i delivered a  character to that they initially  despised but i stuck to my guns with the  character and it seemed to work  while this could be pure hyperbole  considering the circumstances depth's  likely serious for the time being time  will tell when the next parts of the  caribbean project will sail into  theaters but a sing stand at the time of  the johnny depp amber heard verdict  don't expect to see captain jack sparrow  back in action when it does  if you or someone you know is dealing  with domestic abuse you can call the  national domestic violence hotline at  1-800-799-7233  you can also find more information  resources and support at their website  [Music]

